comments:
Circling back - I brought this up in a sig-networking meeting in April (recording is [here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wNPZHoYX2s4&list=PL69nYSiGNLP2E8vmnqo5MwPOY25sDWIxb&t=2200s))

@robscott proposed a path that would piggy back onto @aojea's Cluster IP allocation KEP - where we would provide a way to allocate DNS names.

@thockin had the following points
1. There's a discussion ongoing about Service IP allocation and how it relates to Pod CIDR allocation - this gates the discussion on what we do with DNS
2. Alternatively we can look at the problem more fundamentally (it's an auth issue) and try to creatively come up with a different solution

There was some discussion about considering ReferenceGrant (the one being worked on in sig-auth)
